{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29905 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Phenylmethylsulfonylfluoride (PMF) is implicated in the interaction with prostate cells through a multi-tiered mechanism. The evidence suggests that PMF acts as a target for Caspase-5, which is subsequently targeted by WS-5995 B and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, both of which have a direct effect on prostate cells. This indicates that PMF may influence cellular processes in prostate cells through the Caspase-5 pathway, potentially leading to apoptosis or other programmed cell death mechanisms. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway, including a complex molecular structure that is also a target of PMF, suggests a possible role in modulating cellular signaling in prostate cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for PMF to exert its effects on prostate cells through a well-defined, mechanistically linked sequence of events.",
